<title>GERMANY: Air India adds Germany-US cargo.</title>
<headline>Air India adds Germany-US cargo.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air India has gained limited cargo capacity between Germany and North America with the launch of a twice-weekly Frankfurt to Chicago flight.</p>
<p>The airline said it now flies transatlantic with a Boeing 747-400 aircraft on Thursdays and Saturdays as a continuation of a flight from Bombay.</p>
<p>Return flights to Frankfurt and Bombay are on the same days, a statement said.</p>
<p>Air India said in September that it had gained fifth freedom rights to pick up passengers and cargo in Germany and expected to offer one pallet space. --Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
